      "text": "- 1 . The purpose of the seminar was stated as follows:-\n- 1.1 To bring together experts in the education of industrial designers from several countries to enable them to exchange experience and opinions and discover where common views exist.\n- 1.2 To decide whether it is possible to establish basic principles for the educating of industrial designers which would be valid in all countries in spite of their different stages of industrial development and of their varying appre\u00ad ciation of the need for industrial designers.\n- 1.3 To examine whether there is sufficient agreement on curriculi and me\u00ad thods of educating industrial designers to allow for the giving of specific advice to existing schools and particularly to those concerned with the estab\u00ad lishment of new schools in countries which have, as yet, only elementary or no formal training for industrial designers.\n- 1.4 To consider the future role of the industrial designer in relation to foreseeable developments in industrial technology and the effect this may have on training methods .\n- 1 To consider what steps should be taken to increase the understanding of the proper role of the industrial designer by engineers, management,",
